# =============================================================================
# TEST 123 — AKBASCORE DRA 3.0
#
# LOCAL TRANSPORT CARTOGRAPHY
# SEED-CENTERED FINITE-PROBE ROUTE SELECTION
#
# Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct · BF16 · A100
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CENTRAL QUESTION
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Does a tiny finite perturbation measured ONLY across L11 -> L12 contain
# useful information about which nearby semantic direction will transport
# better to deeper layers, especially L19?
#
#
# IMPORTANT CAUSAL SEPARATION
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# ROUTE SELECTION may see:
#
#       baseline L11
#       baseline L12
#       tiny-probe L12 response
#       locked semantic v12
#
# ROUTE SELECTION may NOT see:
#
#       L13
#       L15
#       L19
#       L27
#
# L19 therefore remains an unseen terminal evaluation endpoint during
# route selection.
#
#
# SEARCH SPACE
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Main candidate cloud:
#
#       q_i = normalize(cos(theta_i) * seed
#                       + sin(theta_i) * u_i)
#
# where:
#
#       u_i ⟂ seed
#
# and theta is frozen to:
#
#       5°, 10°, 15°, 20°, 30°, 45°
#
# 4 orthogonal random deviations per angle:
#
#       6 * 4 = 24 candidates
#
# FIXED seed is evaluated separately.
#
#
# WHY SEED-CENTERED?
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# TEST122 showed that throwing away most of the semantic seed through
# token-cloud PCA projection destroyed transport.
#
# TEST123 therefore preserves semantic identity while asking whether
# small context-specific directional changes around the seed can improve
# transport.
#
#
# PROBE
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Tiny relative injection:
#
#       ||probe|| = PROBE_REL * ||h11||
#
# frozen:
#
#       PROBE_REL = 0.0025
#
# This is 0.25% of hidden-state norm.
#
#
# LOCAL RESPONSE METRICS
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# For candidate q:
#
#       delta12(q) =
#           F11(h11 + eps*q) - F11(h11)
#
# Gain:
#
#       G(q) = ||delta12|| / ||probe11||
#
# Alignment:
#
#       A(q) = cos(delta12, v12)
#
# Signed transport score:
#
#       T(q) = G(q) * A(q)
#
#
# SELECTION
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# TRANSPORT_SELECTED:
#
#       argmax_q T(q)
#
# No coefficient fitting.
# No angle tuning.
# No L19 leakage.
#
#
# FINAL FULL-STRENGTH ARMS
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# 1. FIXED
#       original v11
#
# 2. TRANSPORT_SELECTED
#       candidate with maximum tiny-probe T
#
# 3. CLOUD_RANDOM
#       randomly chosen candidate from the SAME seed-centered cloud
#
# 4. GLOBAL_RANDOM
#       completely random unit direction
#
#
# All four final arms use EXACTLY THE SAME frozen DRA magnitude.
#
#
# PRIMARY ENDPOINT
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#       D19 = cos(delta19, v19)
#
#
# SECONDARY
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#       D12, D13, D15
#       P12, P13, P15, P19, P27
#
# L27 directional metric is raw retention against the injected source
# direction because locked semantic vectors only exist L0-L19.
#
#
# MOST IMPORTANT DIAGNOSTIC
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Across all 24 candidates x 40 prompts:
#
#       correlation(probe T, actual full-strength D19)
#
# BUT:
#
# To avoid using terminal D19 during candidate selection, D19 is measured
# only AFTER the candidate choice is frozen.
#
# For computational cost, full-strength D19 is measured for:
#
#       FIXED
#       SELECTED
#       CLOUD_RANDOM
#       GLOBAL_RANDOM
#
# not all 24 candidates.
#
#
# INTERPRETATION
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Positive result:
#
#   local finite-response measurement contains actionable information
#   for context-conditioned route selection.
#
# Negative result:
#
#   L11->L12 tiny response is insufficient to predict terminal transport.
#
# Neither result proves:
#
#   true Jacobian recovery
#   manifold recovery
#   semantic causality
#   physical momentum / energy transfer
#
# =============================================================================


